<%# AC-23.1: text-only help page covering every member and admin task in the app %>
<section class="bsc-center">
  <h1 class="bsc-title">Help &amp; Support</h1>
  <p class="bsc-sub">How to use the BSC Attendance Portal.</p>

  <div class="bsc-panel bsc-panel--narrow">
    <h2>Signing in</h2>
    <p>
      Press <strong>Sign in with Google</strong> on the home page and choose your official
      TAMU Google account (an address ending in <strong>@tamu.edu</strong>). Personal Gmail
      and other accounts are turned away with an "Access denied" message.
    </p>
    <p>
      The first time you sign in, you'll be asked to complete your profile with your full name,
      your 9-digit UIN, and your class year. You need to save your profile before you can use the
      rest of the app. After that, you stay signed in when you refresh or reopen the page.
    </p>

    <h2>Updating your profile</h2>
    <p>
      Open <strong>User Profile</strong> in the navigation bar to see your details. Press
      <strong>Edit profile</strong> to fix your name, UIN, or class year.
    </p>

    <h2>Checking in to an event</h2>
    <p>
      The <strong>Check-In</strong> page (the home page) lists every event with its date and point
      value. Each event has a tag:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Open</strong>: check-in is available. Tap the event to open it.</li>
      <li><strong>Upcoming</strong>: the event isn't open yet and can't be selected.</li>
      <li><strong>Checked in</strong>: your attendance is already recorded.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Check-in opens 15 minutes before an event starts and closes 3 hours after it starts. On the
      event page, press <strong>Click to check-in</strong>. A checkmark confirms your attendance was
      saved. You can only check in once per event, so pressing the button again won't add extra points.
    </p>
    <p>
      Some events require an optional check-in code set by an admin. If the event page asks for a
      code, get it from a BSC officer at the event and enter it before checking in. If no code is
      required, the code field will not appear.
    </p>

    <h2>Viewing your points</h2>
    <p>
      Every event belongs to a category, such as General Meeting. The top of the home page shows one
      large number per category, side by side. Scroll sideways if there are more than fit on the screen.
      Each number is the points you've earned this semester over the points required, for example
      "2 / 3" under General Meeting. Each event you check in to adds its point value right away. Only
      events from the current semester count.
    </p>

    <h2>Category requirements</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Satisfied</strong> (with a checkmark) means you've earned at least the required points.
        Extra points still show, and the category stays satisfied.
      </li>
      <li><strong>In progress</strong> means you still need more points in that category.</li>
      <li><strong>No requirement</strong> means no requirement is set for that category this semester, so only your earned points show.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      If you see "No active semester", the BSC officers haven't set up a semester yet.
    </p>

    <h2>Appeals</h2>
    <p>
      Open <strong>Appeals</strong> in the navigation to submit an attendance appeal. Choose an event
      from the separate past or upcoming event lists, explain your reason, and submit the form. You may
      attach supporting proof of absence as a PDF, JPG, or PNG smaller than 10 MB; an attachment is
      optional. The page also includes suggestions for avoiding future absences and shows your appeal
      history and each appeal's status.
    </p>

    <h2>For admins</h2>
    <p>
      Admins see <strong>Admin</strong> and <strong>Events</strong> links in the navigation. Changes
      to member access and records should be made carefully; archiving retains records but blocks
      application access.
    </p>
    <h3>Admin</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Use the <strong>Active Members</strong> and <strong>Archived Members</strong> tabs to switch
        between roster lists. The list shows each member's email, UIN, class year, and role.
      </li>
      <li>
        Select <strong>View Details</strong> to see a member's profile, point totals, attendance
        points, administrator adjustment, and event history.
      </li>
      <li>
        From member details, edit profile information or correct the total points. A total-point
        correction preserves attendance records; future check-ins continue adding points.
      </li>
      <li>
        Use <strong>Make Admin</strong> or <strong>Revoke Admin</strong> to change administrator
        access, and confirm the prompt before proceeding.
      </li>
      <li>
        To remove someone from the active roster, open the archive confirmation and check its
        confirmation box. Their records are retained, but their application access is disabled.
      </li>
      <li>
        Under <strong>Pending Attendance Appeals</strong>, select an appeal to review the member's
        reason and event. If proof was attached, use <strong>Download proof of absence</strong>.
        Choose <strong>Approve</strong> or <strong>Deny</strong>: approval records attendance and
        awards the event's points once, including for an upcoming event appeal, while denial leaves
        attendance and points unchanged.
      </li>
      <li>
        Under <strong>Export Member Points</strong>, choose a school year and select
        <strong>Export CSV</strong> to download member point totals for that year (August 1 through
        July 31).
      </li>
    </ul>
    <h3>Events</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Use <strong>Upcoming Events</strong> and <strong>Past Events</strong> to find events.
        Select <strong>Create Event</strong> to add an event or <strong>Edit</strong> to change an
        existing event's details.
      </li>
      <li>
        When creating or editing an event, you may set a <strong>Check-in Code</strong>. Leave it
        blank if no code is needed. If set, members must get the code from an officer and enter it
        on the event check-in page.
      </li>
      <li>
        Events are assigned a category and semester. Their point values count toward the category
        progress shown to members.
      </li>
      <li>
        Under <strong>Manage Categories</strong>, add or rename categories. A category cannot be
        deleted while events or semester requirements use it.
      </li>
      <li>
        Under <strong>Category Requirements</strong>, enter the required points for each category and
        semester, then select <strong>Save Requirements</strong>. Leave a field blank for no
        requirement.
      </li>
      <li>
        Under <strong>Manage Semesters</strong>, create a semester before assigning it to events or
        setting its category requirements. The most recently created semester is treated as current
        for member progress.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Common problems</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>"Access denied" when signing in:</strong> sign in with your @tamu.edu account, not a personal one.</li>
      <li><strong>Sent back to your profile form:</strong> your UIN or class year is missing. Fill them in and save.</li>
      <li><strong>"Isn't open for check-in yet":</strong> wait until 15 minutes before the event starts.</li>
      <li><strong>Points look wrong:</strong> check that the event shows "Checked in" and that it belongs to the expected category and semester. Contact a BSC officer if you still need help.</li>
      <li><strong>An appeal is pending:</strong> an admin must review it. You can check its status in your submitted appeals history.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <% unless logged_in? %>
    <%= link_to "Back to sign in", root_path, class: "bsc-back" %>
  <% end %>
</section>
